# 1. Rotating cube

This first example is a minimal program: a cube that rotates by itself, written in raw OpenGL 3.3 with GLFW
(about 200 lines). The slide sets its speed and its tilt through the address of the frame, and there is no
control on screen. The same source file is compiled for the desktop and for the web.

