## Build and run

*On Windows: see the commands of [Before you start](../01_start/index.html#on-windows).*

On the desktop, from `examples/a1-opengl-cube/`:

```
cmake -S . -B build
cmake --build build
./build/project --speed 0.3 --tilt 40
```

For the web, with the Emscripten SDK activated:

```
emcmake cmake -S . -B build_web
cmake --build build_web
```

`build_web/` then holds `index.html`, `project.js` and `project.wasm`, and the build copies them into `web/` and
`lhtml-site/src/_demo/`: the slides show the new version of the program (to keep `web/` as it is, add
`-DSLIDE_DEMO_PUBLISH=OFF` to the first command). Show the slide through a web server, from the root of the
repository (or of the unzipped folder):

```
python3 -m http.server 8080
```

and open `http://localhost:8080/examples/a1-opengl-cube/slides.html`. After a click in the cube, the right
arrow still goes to the next slide.

